  "formalAccountDeletionMessage": "Official HomaGram account deletion request: Please verify account ownership, explain the deletion process and its consequences, and after identity verification, process the deletion of eligible data in accordance with applicable law.",
  "dataAccessTitle": "Access and obtain a copy",
  "dataAccessBody": "To request a copy of information associated with your account, contact us through in-app support. Submit the request from the same account so ownership can be verified.",
  "dataCorrectionTitle": "Correct your information",
  "dataCorrectionBody": "You can update your display name, username, and editable profile details in profile editing. For information that cannot be changed directly, contact support.",
  "dataDeletionBody": "To request account deletion, use in-app support. Before deletion, we will explain its consequences, information that may need to be retained by law or to handle reports and disputes, and what happens to published content. This page does not delete your account by itself.",
  "dataRequestReviewTitle": "Review and follow-up",
  "dataRequestReviewBody": "Requests are reviewed after verifying identity and the scope of the request. Never share your sign-in details, password, or one-time code with anyone.",
  "aboutMissionTitle": "HomaGram — Connection Beyond Boundaries",
  "aboutMissionBody": "HomaGram is a social and multimedia messaging space designed to bring people, ideas, and experiences closer together—a place to talk, discover content, and build meaningful connections.",
  "aboutFeaturesTitle": "A home for connection and creativity",
  "aboutFeaturesBody": "Share photos and videos, watch Reels and Stories, chat, create groups and channels, comment, and follow content you enjoy. Our goal is to bring everyday communication experiences together in one coherent, thoughtfully designed space.",
  "aboutExperienceTitle": "Designed for a smooth experience",
  "aboutExperienceBody": "From visual identity to interface motion, we aim to provide an experience that feels fast, readable, and welcoming. HomaGram evolves continuously, and new features are made available after staged testing and review.",
  "aboutPrivacyTitle": "Privacy and user control",
  "aboutPrivacyBody": "Private-account controls, information visibility settings, session management, content reporting, and support access are part of how we build trust. Never share your password or sign-in code. Details about data processing are available in Privacy and Security.",
  "aboutCommunityTitle": "A community built on respect",
  "aboutCommunityBody": "HomaGram is built for respectful conversation and creative participation. Safety, dignity, and other people's rights should be respected when publishing and communicating. Valid reports are reviewed, and support is available for follow-up.",
  "aboutRoadmapTitle": "Development vision",
  "aboutRoadmapBody": "HomaGram's development focuses on messaging, profile experience, content creation tools, account security, accessibility, and performance. Features in development are not product promises until they are released and tested.",
  "aboutContactTitle": "Contact the HomaGram team",
  "aboutContactBody": "For suggestions, bug reports, review requests, or account questions, use in-app support. If your report includes screenshots or private information, send only what is necessary.",
  "aboutIdentityTitle": "Product identity",
  "aboutIdentityBody": "HomaGram • Connection Beyond Boundaries",
  "policyTerms1Title": "1. Acceptance and legal framework",
  "policyTerms1Body": "Using HomaGram means accepting these Terms and the Privacy Policy. These terms are prepared with regard to applicable laws of the Islamic Republic of Iran, including relevant constitutional provisions, the Civil Code, the E-Commerce Law, and the Computer Crimes Law. Mandatory legal provisions prevail in case of conflict.",
  "policyTerms2Title": "2. Eligibility and responsible use",
  "policyTerms2Body": "Users must have the legal capacity required to create an account and undertake related legal acts. Articles 956–960 of the Civil Code provide the general framework for the beginning and end of legal capacity and the exercise of civil rights. Where the law requires consent or action by a parent, guardian, or legal representative, the user and their legal guardian are responsible for complying.",
  "policyTerms3Title": "3. Accurate information and account security",
  "policyTerms3Body": "Account information must be accurate and kept up to date where possible. Users are responsible for protecting their devices and sign-in credentials and must not share passwords, one-time codes, or security keys. Impersonation, unauthorized access, account trading, and attempts to bypass security measures are prohibited.",
  "policyTerms4Title": "4. Permitted content and publishing responsibility",
  "policyTerms4Body": "Users are responsible for content they publish or send and must respect others’ rights, privacy, intellectual property, and applicable law. Threats, harassment, disclosure of private information, fraud, spam, impersonation, malware, unlawful content, and exploitative or sexual content involving minors are prohibited.",
  "policyTerms5Title": "5. Content ownership and limited service license",
  "policyTerms5Body": "To the extent provided by law, users retain the rights to content they create. Users grant HomaGram only a limited, non-exclusive license to host, store, display, transmit, back up, and provide features they choose, to the extent necessary for those purposes. This license does not transfer ownership and ends upon deletion of the content or account, subject to technical feasibility and legal obligations.",
  "policyTerms6Title": "6. Communications and respect for privacy",
  "policyTerms6Body": "Private messages and communications must not be disclosed to others without authorization or lawful authority. Article 22 of the Constitution protects the dignity, rights, and privacy of individuals, while Article 25 prohibits interference with correspondence and communications except as provided by law. Users must not use HomaGram tools to threaten, harass, or violate privacy.",
  "policyTerms7Title": "7. Reports, review, and protective actions",
  "policyTerms7Body": "Users may report content, messages, or suspicious behavior. HomaGram reviews reports and, depending on the severity and recurrence of a violation, may restrict or remove content, temporarily disable features, or suspend an account. Where possible, the reason and review process will be communicated. These measures do not replace the authority of legal bodies.",
  "policyTerms8Title": "8. Intellectual property and third-party rights",
  "policyTerms8Body": "You may upload another person’s work only if you own it, have valid permission, or are otherwise legally authorized. Rights holders or their legal representatives may submit the content URL, a description of the claimed right, and supporting evidence through support. False reports or misuse of the reporting process are also prohibited.",
  "policyTerms9Title": "9. Availability and liability",
  "policyTerms9Body": "The service may be temporarily unavailable due to maintenance, internet disruptions, security incidents, or factors beyond our control. HomaGram takes reasonable steps to reduce disruptions and protect data but does not guarantee uninterrupted availability or absolute security. Nothing in this section excludes liability that cannot lawfully be waived.",
  "policyTerms10Title": "10. Requests and dispute resolution",
  "policyTerms10Body": "For questions, appeals of moderation decisions, or account-related requests, first contact in-app support. The right to seek relief before competent authorities, as recognized by Article 34 of the Constitution, remains unaffected. Governing law and jurisdiction are determined subject to applicable jurisdictional rules and mandatory provisions.",
  "policyTerms11Title": "11. Changes and current version",
  "policyTerms11Body": "Material changes to these terms will be communicated through in-app notices or another appropriate method. The review date and current version will be shown in this section. Continued use after changes take effect is subject to the updated terms to the extent permitted by law.",
  "policyPrivacy1Title": "1. Scope and protection principles",
  "policyPrivacy1Body": "HomaGram processes information to provide and secure its social and messaging services. This policy is prepared with regard to Articles 22 and 25 of the Constitution and Articles 58–61 of the E-Commerce Law concerning the protection of personal data messages.",
  "policyPrivacy2Title": "2. Information we process",
  "policyPrivacy2Body": "Depending on the features you use, we may process account and authentication details, your name and username, profile photo and bio, posts, Reels, Stories, comments, messages, uploaded files, connection lists, reports, settings, and necessary security records.",
  "policyPrivacy3Title": "3. Technical information and error reports",
  "policyPrivacy3Body": "To diagnose issues and protect the service, we may record information such as device model and operating-system version, app version, event time, technical logs, and identifiers needed for troubleshooting. Screenshots or attachments are sent only when you knowingly select and submit them.",
  "policyPrivacy4Title": "4. Purpose and data minimization",
  "policyPrivacy4Body": "Information is used to create and operate accounts, display content, provide messaging and notifications, offer support, prevent abuse, review reports, and improve performance. Under Article 59 of the E-Commerce Law, processing purposes must be clear and data must not be used beyond what is necessary or for an undisclosed purpose.",
  "policyPrivacy5Title": "5. Sensitive information and consent",
  "policyPrivacy5Body": "Do not submit sensitive information about yourself or others unless genuinely necessary and legally authorized. Article 58 of the E-Commerce Law prohibits processing certain sensitive data without the person’s explicit consent. HomaGram must not use sensitive data for purposes beyond those disclosed.",
  "policyPrivacy6Title": "6. Public visibility and private communications",
  "policyPrivacy6Body": "Posts or information you publish publicly may be visible to and reshared by other users. Private messages are designed to be available only to participants in that conversation; however, recipients may save or report content they receive. Do not send sign-in details or security codes in messages.",
  "policyPrivacy7Title": "7. Sharing with providers and legal authorities",
  "policyPrivacy7Body": "We may use infrastructure providers for hosting, databases, file storage, authentication, and notifications; their access should be limited to what is needed to provide the service. User information is not sold. Disclosure to legal authorities occurs only within the scope of valid requests and applicable legal requirements.",
  "policyPrivacy8Title": "8. Retention, deletion, and backups",
  "policyPrivacy8Body": "Information is retained for as long as needed to provide the service, maintain security, resolve disputes, or meet legal obligations. After an account-deletion request, eligible data enters the deletion process. Data that must be retained by law or for a valid security need is kept with restricted access and only for that purpose. Backups may remain until their technical retention cycle ends.",
  "policyPrivacy9Title": "9. Access, correction, and deletion requests",
  "policyPrivacy9Body": "Users may use account tools or support to access their information, correct inaccurate data, obtain a copy, or request deletion. Article 59 of the E-Commerce Law addresses, among other things, an individual's access to their information file and the ability to correct or request erasure. Requests are handled after account ownership is verified and legal exceptions are considered.",
  "policyPrivacy10Title": "10. Security and access controls",
  "policyPrivacy10Body": "Appropriate technical and organizational measures, such as access controls, authentication, secure communications, and necessary event logging, are used to protect information. No system is completely secure; report suspicious incidents through support.",
  "policyPrivacy11Title": "11. Rights of younger users",
  "policyPrivacy11Body": "Features and processing involving younger users must comply with applicable laws and any requirements for consent or supervision by a parent or legal guardian. Users must not publish a minor’s contact details, address, school, location, or private images without authorization.",
  "policyPrivacy12Title": "12. Legal basis and updates",
  "policyPrivacy12Body": "This policy is based, among other things, on Articles 22, 25, and 34 of the Constitution; Articles 956–960 of the Civil Code concerning legal capacity; Articles 58–61 of the E-Commerce Law; and relevant provisions of the Computer Crimes Law. Interpretation and application are subject to the authoritative texts and amendments in force when a matter is reviewed.",
  "policyCommunity1Title": "Respect and safety",
  "policyCommunity1Body": "Threats, stalking, persistent harassment, targeted humiliation, hate speech, and disclosure of private addresses or contact information are prohibited.",
  "policyCommunity2Title": "Content and authenticity",
  "policyCommunity2Body": "Impersonation, spam, fraud, malware, unlawful content, intellectual-property infringement, and unauthorized disclosure of private information are prohibited.",
  "policyCommunity3Title": "Protecting minors",
  "policyCommunity3Body": "Any exploitation, threats, requests for sexual content, or inappropriate contact involving minors are prohibited. Do not save or redistribute child-abuse material; report it immediately.",
  "policyCommunity4Title": "Reporting and content review",
  "policyCommunity4Body": "Reports must be submitted honestly and in good faith. Reports concerning offensive political content and content that violates laws or regulations are reviewed and followed up by the support team within 24 hours at most. If a violation is confirmed, the content will be removed or access restricted in accordance with applicable rules. Accurate and responsible user reports help identify violations sooner and maintain a safe, respectful HomaGram environment. Knowingly false reports or using reporting tools to harass others may result in account restrictions.",
  "policyCopyright1Title": "Rights in creative works",
  "policyCopyright1Body": "Music, photos, videos, text, and trademarks may be protected by intellectual-property rights. Upload only content you own or are validly licensed to use.",
  "policyCopyright2Title": "Submit a claim",
  "policyCopyright2Body": "A rights holder or authorized representative may submit the content URL, a description of the claimed right, contact details, and supporting evidence through support.",
  "policyCopyright3Title": "Actions and review",
  "policyCopyright3Body": "After an appropriate review, content may be restricted or removed. Repeated violations may lead to account restrictions. Affected users may submit an explanation and counter-evidence."
}
